				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zesc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5703022); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5703022&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607353157" alt="Zesc" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5703022)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zesc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5703022); return false;" >Zesc</a></span> <span class="odate time_1570899894 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">12 Oct 2019 17:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4397075">
									

<p>I'm feeling like there was some potential wasted with this. The main idea is intriguing enough, i especially like that it's mostly a &quot;mundane&quot; conspiracy with non-anomalous participants that just happen to possess an anomaly they can use.</p>
<p>However, there are quite a few plot hick-ups on this. DrMagnus summed it up quite nicely over a year ago, but there are two other things i wish to mention:</p>
<ol>
<li>There is this line &quot;<tt>a general consensus among site staff led to a request for an in-depth investigation of the American government and past cabinet officials</tt>&quot; which broke my suspension of disbelief. Depending on how it is read, it either means the SCP Foundation has to ask the US government for permission to investigate them, or that they need an allowance to do something every investigative journalist could do from their home office. And why a consensu of site staff? Isn't this something for a Site Director or Senior Researcher to decide?</li>
</ol>
<ol>
<li>The overall inclusion of <a href="/scp-1867">SCP-1867</a>. Think of cross-links whatever you want, this one is seems like a cheap origin story. Actually, having no explanation of how the Foundation learned of this could have helped the flow of the story, and leave some mystery. Especially that it is speaking of events past 1910 (which is against the original scip) and the added headcanon regarding its contact with Roosevelt is something i find slightly off-putting.</li>
</ol>
<p>I still like the idea and execution good enough to stay at a neutral vote.</p>

